  "FormatVersion": 1,
  "comment": "Maps Virtual Church Musician GitHub release assets to matrix entries. {tag}=v1.0.1-b.7, {ver}=1.0.1-b.7, {base}=1.0.1. public:false entries are never published; server and midi-player are public (uploaded and hashed into matrix.json) so alpha/beta testers can fetch them through the password-gated flow in download_handler, but the Lambda still blocks them outright once a release's channel is 'stable' -- see PASSWORD_REQUIRED_APPS in src/download_handler/handler.py. signing: apple = macOS notarization (attested by the workflow input), authenticode = Windows signature (detected), apk = a non-debug signing certificate (detected), none = not required. An asset can be a list of alternative file names (the first one present in the release is used): the applications were renamed for v1.0.1-b.9 (see APP_RENAME_MAPPING.md in the VCM repo), so releases from before that keep the old name.",
